          "unit": "text"
        }
      ],
      "referenceData": [
        {
          "topic": "Scope",
          "instructions": "The authored street-team deployments with fixed deployment charges and same-day timing. Supply venue staffing, access, spending and contribution inputs; customer response is not forecast."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Starting values",
          "instructions": "Prefilled values are fictional examples. Changing part of the workbook can leave example inputs in the case."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Editing",
          "instructions": "Edit the named input sheets. Keep worksheet names, column headers and record identifiers. Do not add formulas. Other case inputs remain unchanged."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Units and time",
          "instructions": "Clock fields use HH:mm on the operating date. USD fields display dollars. Customer travel remains a duration."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Import",
          "instructions": "Upload this workbook, inspect the changes and diagnostics, then apply. Importing does not calculate results or establish operating permission."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Qualified staffing and operatin",
          "instructions": "Editable inputs. Same venue, event and operating date. Count only staff qualified and available throughout the complete absence; unavailable staff are subtracted once."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Promotion timing",
          "instructions": "Editable inputs. Use local minutes from midnight on the operating date. Customer travel time assumes the guest accepts the offer; it does not predict acceptance."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Promotion expense and spending ",
          "instructions": "Editable inputs. USD cents. Each plan quote includes its full additional expense. The spending limit and delegated permission are separate from approval of the chosen plan."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Venue contribution per addition",
          "instructions": "Editable inputs. USD cents retained by the venue per additional guest after the offer and variable costs. Additional means a visit caused by the promotion; returning customers can count. A visit attributed to an offer is not necessarily additional. Unknown remains unknown; zero or negative contribution cannot cover a positive cost. Break-even counts cover the plan’s additional expense plus any separate existing-customer discount loss."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Separate discount loss on exist",
          "instructions": "Editable inputs. USD cents of additional contribution lost on guests who would have attended anyway. Include only loss not already counted in guest contribution or the plan’s expense. Break-even counts cover additional expense plus this separate loss. Unknown leaves the guest target unassessed."
        }
      ]
